{
  "_about": "Shared cases of to_analysis (plan E2.3-E2.6, D3, WP64; the TypeScript inverse of WP80 must agree). INPUTS of every case: its 'query' and the top-level 'catalog' (kind and field types per layer, as the controls know them from the layer list; modelled on the sample data, with date fields added). A query is representable exactly when to_analysis finds an analysis and resultQuery of that analysis (frontend/src/analysis/query.ts) has the query's canonical form. 'analysis' is the query part of the frontend state (QueryPart of analysis/model.ts: result, tree, restriction) plus the result layer's symbology; node ids are left out and not compared. The controls' limits: the result is a vector layer; a row names a field of its layer with an operator operatorsFor (editor/describe.ts) offers for the field's type, a number range only on a number field, a date range only on a date field; a relation or reference names another vector layer, never the result layer; a relation's filter is one attribute row of the related layer, never negated (no NICHT toggle there). The model path adds: no restriction ('bbox', 'geometry': the map's, never the model's), no symbology, no 'not' of a 'not' (the draft of a proposal, frontend/src/model/panel/draft.ts, takes none of them; a representable case gives a draft whose resultQuery is the case's query, tested in frontend/src/model/represent.test.ts). Where several analyses give one query, to_analysis picks: the root is an 'and' group, never negated, an 'and' at the top gives the root's children; 'not' of 'within' is 'outside', of 'dwithin' 'far', otherwise 'not' sets the node's flag; 'and' of a 'ge' and a 'le' compare on one date field with ISO dates in order is one date range row. 'conditions' is the count the limit of the model path uses (MAX_CONDITIONS 8, also for a follow-up's analysis, P6): one per row of the tree (an attribute row, a date range row, a relation with its filter, a reference row) and one for a restriction (none on the model path); groups, and, or, not count nothing. 'part' of a case that is not representable names the first top-level field (in schema order) or condition op the controls cannot show; it is the refusal's details.part.",
